WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.480
An automated setup prepares the fictional product's 14-hour battery draft.

2
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.180
That draft's recorded approval places its text on the demo catalogue.

3
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:18.180
Typed by Claude (automated test): battery changes to 12 hours.

4
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.160
The decision identifies the exact older text version.

5
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:50.200
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the merchandiser.

6
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:57.060
The workflow holds the older draft because its source attributes changed.

7
00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:04.300
The corrected draft says 12 hours and replaces the older waiting draft.

8
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:22.380
The demo catalogue retains the approved text while the corrected draft waits.
